3. Reaffirms that the measures referred to in paragraph 1 are intended to target individuals and entities designated by the Committee and are not directed against the people of Mali, are without prejudice to the primary responsibility of the Transition Government of Mali to protect civilians and combat terrorism in accordance with its international obligations, including international human rights law and international humanitarian law, are implemented in full compliance with international law, and do not prevent the delivery of humanitarian assistance by impartial humanitarian actors in accordance with international humanitarian law, and do not impede the fight against impunity;
