5. Requests the Panel of Experts to continue to cooperate closely with the Transition Government of Mali, the Committee and relevant stakeholders, and, as appropriate, regional and subregional organizations, including the African Union and ECOWAS, to gather, examine and analyse information on the implementation of the measures, and to include in its reporting information on the implementation of the measures, including human rights violations and abuses, violations of international humanitarian law, obstruction of the Agreement and impediments to humanitarian access, as well as the humanitarian impact of the measures, while ensuring that its reporting remains objective, evidence-based and balanced and maintaining its independence and impartiality;
6. Calls upon all Member States to cooperate fully with the Committee and the Panel of Experts, including by providing information on the implementation of the measures;
7. Reaffirms its support for the Agreement on Peace and Reconciliation in Mali emanating from the Algiers process, and calls upon all parties to the Agreement to accelerate its implementation and to refrain from any action that could undermine peace and reconciliation;
8. Stresses the importance of the full, equal and meaningful participation of women and youth in the political transition and in the implementation of the Agreement;
9. Calls upon the Transition Government of Mali and all relevant parties to cooperate fully with the United Nations, and to ensure that the withdrawal of MINUSMA and the transfer of its tasks are conducted in an orderly and safe manner, in full respect of the Status of Forces Agreement until the departure of the final element of MINUSMA from Mali, including by ensuring the safety, security and freedom of movement of United Nations personnel and unimpeded access to United Nations facilities, in close coordination with the United Nations and troop- and police-contributing countries, and as appropriate with the United Nations Country Team and UNOWAS; and calls upon all parties to protect civilians, respect international humanitarian law and human rights law, and ensure safe and unhindered humanitarian access throughout the withdrawal and transfer of tasks;
