11. Calls upon all parties, including all security personnel operating in Mali, to ensure that all operations, including joint operations, are conducted in full compliance with international humanitarian law and human rights law and to take all feasible precautions to protect civilians;
12. Decides that the measures renewed by this resolution shall be reviewed by 31 March 2024, taking into account progress in the political transition, the implementation of the Agreement, the security and humanitarian situation, respect for human rights and international humanitarian law, and the reports of the Panel of Experts, bearing in mind the designation criteria in resolution 2374 (2017), with a view to considering the continuation or adjustment of the measures as appropriate;
